# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=conquest spec=priest:shadow
# style=idle view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and every .play under playtest/plans/ first: no
# mode=battleground session anywhere on record has ever used style=idle, on
# any map. direction.md's #7 ("a battleground does not carry a passive body
# the way a raid does") so far only has flee/dodge (zero presses, but the
# style still actively steers the body away from danger), good/melee/mash
# (presses, with or without steering) and auto (presses only what the bar
# allows). None of those is the direct mirror of #1's raid finding, where
# `idle` means literally nothing: no presses AND no movement at all, stick
# released the whole time. This is the first chance to run that exact
# control on a battleground and see whether a body that does nothing dies
# passively (as flee/dodge's untouched-the-whole-match readings suggest a
# truly inert body might) or gets found and killed regardless (as #7's shape
# for active-but-doomed styles suggests). Three chunks with `bill` after each
# to watch the trend rather than one end-state snapshot.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:priest:shadow
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play idle 90
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play idle 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play idle 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
